#X text 59 148 If an argument has been supplied \, it will appear as a list \, and [route] will send that list ("[symbol argument(" ) out the right outlet. If no argument has been supplied \, only the word "symbol" will be delivered to [route] \, and it will not be interpreted as a list \, thus sending this data out the right outlet., f 38;
#X text 49 378 The list from [route]'s right outlet is converted back to a symbol and sent to the outlet. The message from [route]'s right outlet is just the message [symbol( \, so we use that to trigger a "bang" which causes the [symbol default] object to output the symbol "default" \, which is send to the outlet., f 37;
